      "answer": "**Similarities**  \n- Both PTO and sick leave are paid time\u2011off benefits provided to full\u2011time employees.  \n- Each type of leave is allocated on a yearly basis (per calendar year).  \n\n**Differences**  \n- **Amount:** Employees receive 22 days of PTO per year, while they receive 10 paid sick days per year.\u202f[S1]  \n- **Accrual:** PTO is accrued at a rate of 1.83 days per month; sick leave is not described as accruing monthly.\u202f[S1]  \n- **Carry\u2011over:** Up to 5 unused PTO days may be carried over to the next year (but must be used by March\u202f31); sick days do **not** carry over.\u202f[S1]  \n\n**Conclusion**  \nBoth PTO and sick leave are paid annual benefits, but PTO provides a larger number of days, accrues monthly, and allows limited carry\u2011over, whereas sick leave offers fewer days, does not accrue monthly, and cannot be carried over. All relevant information is present in the evidence; no side is missing.\u202f[S1]",
